 ction\n\n*********************************\n\n[Uploaded Image] (https://by
 u.instructure.com/courses/36994/files/13577535/download?download_frd=1&hid
 den=1)\n\n \n\nThis assignment is due by Friday at 11:59 p.m.\n\n--------
 -------\n   Instructions\n---------------\n\nWrite a one-paragraph (appr
 ox. 250 words) reflection on what you hope to learn about humanity through
  the lens of anthropology. \n\nAs you consider how anthropology can help 
 us better understand people\, cultures\, societies\, and shared experience
 s across time and place\, you could write about: \n\n* Questions you have
  about humanity \n\n* Topics you are curious about \n\n* Ways you think 
 anthropology might change how you view yourself and others \n\n* How anth
 ropology might be useful to you in your personal and professional endeavor
 s \n\nNo AI may be used for this assignment. Your response should be orig
 inal\, thoughtful\, focused\, and written in complete sentences. Be sure t
 o connect your reflection directly to anthropology and what you hope to ga
 in from studying it. \n\n------------\n  Submission\n------------\n\nAf
 ter completing your reflection\n\nSubmit your completed work\, on this sub
 mission page\, in one of the following formats:\n\n* .doc\n\n* .docx\n\n 
 \n\nImage Credits\n-------------\n\nAgusCami/stock.adobe.com\, [Panorama o
 f Puka Pukara ruins (or Puca Pucara) near Cusco\, thought to be a military
  base and administrative center of the late inca empire. Beautiful travel 
 destination in the Sacred Valley\, Peru] (https://stock.adobe.com/images/p
 anorama-of-puka-pukara-ruins-or-puca-pucara-near-cusco-thought-to-be-a-mil
 itary-base-and-administrative-center-of-the-late-inca-empire-beautiful-tra
 vel-destination-in-the-sacred-valley-peru/273763015?prev_url=detail)[Links
  to an external site.] (https://stock.adobe.com/search?k=broken+pots&searc
 h_type=usertyped&filters%5Bgentech%5D=exclude&asset_id=143131592)\, (Adobe
  Stock Education License). [Image has been altered from the original.]\n\n
