  an artifact (physical object) that represents you.\n\n* Write a brief exp
 lanation of yourself (about 3-4 sentences) and how this artifact represent
 s an aspect of your identity and who you are.\n\n \n\nBy the Friday of we
 ek 2 at 11:59 pm\, respond to at least two group members using the foll
 owing instructions:\n\n* Identify artifacts that you connect with or that 
 resonate with you.\n\n* For both group members\, comment on their post and
  how your feel connected to their artifact. For example\, you can use one 
 of the prompts below to begin your comment:\n\n*\n\n* Your artifact remind
 s me of ________.\n\n* I had a similar artifact that ________.\n\n* This a
 rtifact is symbolic of an experience I had where ________.\n\n* This conne
 cts to the gospel of Jesus Christ because ________.\n\n \n\nTip: Revisit 
 your post at some point and see how classmates connected to your artifact 
 in similar or different ways. Take advantage of this great opportunity to 
 get to know your group\, with whom you'll be working throughout the course
 .\n\n \n\nImage Credits\n-------------\n\nChatGPT\, response to "5:1 bann
